You are working in OpenBot, a thin local board that routes work to Hermes Agent and OpenCode. You are not building a third agent engine.

Before any edit:
1. Read OPENBOT.md, AGENTS.md, and brains/INDEX.md.
2. Then read ARCHITECTURE.md, BRAND.md, BROWSER.md if the task touches cost, credit, or browser.

Hard rules:
- Wire official `hermes` and `opencode` binaries. Do not clone those repos into this tree.
- Chat is UI. brains/INDEX.md is memory. Thread JSON is never the prompt.
- Cos has no tools. MCP only on Builder when the user toggles it.
- Name the engine on every job card.
- Required credit on README, footer, first-run: OpenBot uses Hermes Agent (MIT, Nous Research) and OpenCode (MIT, Anomaly). Not affiliated with, sponsored by, or endorsed by those projects.
- No secrets in git.
- Week 1 scope only unless the user explicitly asks for Week 2+.

First prompt to implement if the board is incomplete: detect engines, serve http://127.0.0.1:8787, status path reads INDEX, code path calls `opencode run` when present.
